`crimes context` confirms all three findings and reports no nearby tests. I’d refactor the card into a non-interactive layout container with an explicit action:

```tsx
type CardProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate: () => void;
};

export function Card({ children, onActivate }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <article className="@container w-full max-w-screen-lg border border-card-border bg-surface p-6 text-ink shadow-sm">
      <div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 @md:grid-cols-3">
        <div className="min-w-0 text-base @md:col-span-2 @md:text-lg">
          {children}
        </div>

        <aside className="min-w-0 text-sm text-muted">sidebar</aside>
      </div>

      <button
        type="button"
        className="mt-6 rounded bg-brand px-4 py-2 text-surface focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand"
        onClick={onActivate}
      >
        Open card
      </button>
    </article>
  );
}
```

How this maps to the findings:

- `accessible_interaction_risk`: Replace the clickable `<div>` with a native `<button>`. This provides keyboard activation, focusability, and button semantics automatically. Because `children` is arbitrary React content, wrapping the entire card in a button could create invalid nested interactions; an explicit action is safer. If the action navigates, use `<a href>` instead.
- `design_token_escape`: Replace inline colors, spacing, shadow, and focus values with Tailwind tokens. Reuse `brand`, `surface`, and `ink`; add semantic `card-border` and `muted` tokens to `tailwind.config.ts`. If the magenta background is intentional, create a named card/accent token rather than copying `#ff00aa`.
- `responsive_fragility`: Remove the fixed `800`, `720`, `600`, and `240` dimensions. `w-full` plus `max-w-screen-lg` makes the outer card fluid, while the container-responsive grid collapses to one column and expands to a 2:1 layout when space permits. Tokenized `text-base`/`text-lg` replaces raw `18px`.

I would also add a component test confirming the action is discoverable by role and activates with both keyboard and pointer input. No files were changed.
